[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=18198)[0m (""Sous le dôme épais"") for sopranos performed in Act 1 by Lakmé, the daughter of a Brahmin priest, and her servant Mallika. The name ""Lakmé"" is the French rendition of Sanskrit Lakshmi, the name of the Hindu Goddess of Wealth. The opera's most famous aria is the ""Bell Song"" (""L'Air des clochettes"") in Act 2. Like other French operas of the period, ""Lakmé"" captures the ambience of the Orient seen through Western eyes, which was periodically in vogue during the latter part of the 19th ce
